{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"5e05091a-aa53-4a37-bfda-6eba49b21a80","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have updated the prompt caching configuration and documented the changes in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-umDBfQ/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n- In [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-umDBfQ/bot.py), modified `build_system(a, today)` to return two distinct system prompt text blocks, each marked with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`:\n  1. **Segment 1**: The byte-stable coaching `INSTRUCTIONS` (~780 tokens).\n  2. **Segment 2**: The volatile `athlete_context(a, today)` (~240–300 tokens: date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language).\n- Because Anthropic prompt caching uses a prefix hash, splitting these into two blocks ensures that updates from `save_fact` only invalidate and re-cache the volatile tail segment, preserving the cached static instruction prefix across calls.\n\nSee [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-umDBfQ/ANSWER.md) for full details on the changes and which parts of the colleague's note applied versus were ignored.\n","duration_seconds":47.076206,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":94767,"output_tokens":1863,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":140790,"total_tokens":96630}}}
